[subsection {quic}]

The quic module provides the experimental HTTP/3 network driver based
 on QUIC. It is part of NaviServer 5.1, but requires OpenSSL 4.0 or newer.
 The driver uses an existing HTTPS driver configuration as a fallback
 for shared network-driver and TLS settings. Values specified in the
 HTTP/3 section override the corresponding HTTPS values, allowing TCP
 and UDP drivers to use different transport and thread settings.

[para]
 HTTP/3 support is disabled by default. The current implementation is
 functional but still experimental and not yet recommended for
 production use. More testing, leak checking, load testing, and
 hardening are still needed.


[para]
This module also accepts the parameters documented for [const "nsssl"]. The parameters listed below are specific to [const "quic"].

[para]
This module should be loaded globally through [const ns/modules].

[example_begin]
 ns_section ns/modules {
     ns_param https nsssl
     ns_param h3    quic
 }

 ns_section ns/module/https {
     ns_param port        8443
     ns_param certificate /usr/local/ns/certificates/server.pem

     # Extra parameters specific for HTTP/3
     # ns_param h3advertise    true
     # ns_param h3persist      false
 }
 ns_section ns/module/h3 {
     ns_param https                 ns/module/https
     # ns_param driverthreads       2
     ns_param writerthreads         1
     ns_param recvbufsize           8MB
     ns_param sendbufsize           8MB
     ns_param sendqueuesize         256kB
     ns_param idletimeout           3s
     ns_param draintimeout          10ms
     ns_param validateclientaddress true
 }
[example_end]

[para]
For detailed documentation, see [uri ../../quic/files/quic.html {quic}].

[list_begin definitions]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "debug"]"]
Enable detailed HTTP/3 and QUIC diagnostic logging

[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "boolean"]
[item] Default: [const "false"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "draintimeout"]"]

                    Drain timeout used when closing QUIC connections,
                    allowing pending packets or connection-close
                    handling to complete


[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "time"]
[item] Default: [const "10ms"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "https"]"]

                    Configuration section of the HTTPS driver to which
                    this HTTP/3 driver is linked. Shared driver and TLS
                    parameters fall back to values from this section;
                    parameters specified in ns/module/h3 override them


[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "section"]
[item] Default: [const "ns/module/https"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "idletimeout"]"]
Maximum idle time for QUIC connections before they are closed

[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "time"]
[item] Default: [const "3s"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "maxudppayloadsize"]"]

                    Maximum UDP payload size advertised to the peer as the
                    QUIC max_udp_payload_size transport parameter. Valid
                    values range from 1200 to 65527 bytes. This parameter
                    requires OpenSSL 4.1 or newer.

                    Currently, the setting only changes the advertised
                    transport parameter. OpenSSL neither uses it to increase
                    outgoing QUIC packet sizes nor enforces it as a receive
                    limit, so it currently has no direct operational effect.


[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "size"]
[item] Default: [const "1200"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "port"]"]
UDP port or ports on which the HTTP/3 driver listens

[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "integer"]
[item] Default: [const "443"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "recvbufsize"]"]
Size of the UDP receive buffer used by the HTTP/3 driver

[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "size"]
[item] Default: [const "8MB"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "sendbufsize"]"]
Size of the UDP send buffer used by the HTTP/3 driver (SO_SNDBUF). A value of 0 leaves the operating system default unchanged. The effective size is subject to operating system limits

[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "size"]
[item] Default: [const "8MB"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "sendqueuesize"]"]

                    Maximum response-body data retained in the HTTP/3
                    stream send queue. When this limit is reached, writer
                    delivery pauses until the queue drains to half the
                    configured size.


[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "size"]
[item] Default: [const "256kB"]
[list_end]

[def "Parameter name: [emph "validateclientaddress"]"]

                    Validate the QUIC client address before accepting a new
                    connection. Clients without a valid address-validation token
                    receive a Retry packet, adding one network round trip. Disabling
                    validation improves first-connection latency but weakens protection
                    against spoofed-source connection floods.


[list_begin itemized]
[item] Type: [const "boolean"]
[item] Default: [const "true"]
[list_end]

[list_end]
